BT 1 0 0 1 0 108.75 Tm 13.25 TL 0 0 0 rg /F2+0 10.5 Tf 13.25 TL (We release eight executable historical-data repair contracts across six Python projects, covering 65 historical files) Tj T* (and 252 dependent observations of reading, continued use and persistence. The resource calibrates acceptance) Tj T* -0.022477 Tw (when an old format has lost information. Two source repairs satisfy all 84 observations of a jsonpickle contract, yet) Tj T* 0 Tw (literal equality with the reference rejects 60 observations for one valid repair. A corrupting control satisfies none) Tj T* (despite completing every load and restart. All eight upstream-derived backports pass their contracts. Of 32) Tj T* (completed Gemma 4 repair attempts, four satisfy both semantic checks and source review. Released artifacts) Tj T* (include historical bytes, patches, retained failures and an API-free verifier. The contribution is an executable) Tj T* (resource of eight repair contracts and an acceptance calibration, grounded in a known upstream ambiguity. Code,) Tj T* (data and paper: ) Tj .117647 .270588 .341176 rg (https://github.com/GuilinDev/historical-data-repair-contracts/releases/tag/v0.1.1) Tj T* ET
